course: dictionary
lesson: 4764
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word housekeeping can mean the work of looking after a home, or the money set aside to run one. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant. Ask: what is the topic here, and which meaning would make sense?
explain: «Mum gave me the housekeeping to buy the food.» The words money and buy are the clues, so housekeeping means the money for running the home. Now try another sentence: «Housekeeping in the hotel starts at seven.» Here the clue is hotel, so housekeeping means the team that cleans the rooms.
explain: An old story says Toad came back «fresh and gay, remarking what a pleasant easy life it was», after «the cares and worries and fatigues of housekeeping at home». Gay here means cheerful, which is its old meaning. Housekeeping means the everyday jobs of looking after a home, and the clue is that these jobs felt like worries and fatigue.
fact: Housekeeping means the work of looking after a home: cleaning, cooking, shopping and paying bills.
fact: In hotels and hospitals, housekeeping is the department that cleans the rooms.
fact: Housekeeping can also mean money set aside for running a home.
fact: In an organisation, informal housekeeping means small tidy-up jobs, such as updating files or checking dates. At meetings you might hear «a few housekeeping notes before we start».
fact: In stories, Mole takes pride in his housekeeping, and Rat is a good housekeeper.
exercise: «Mum gave me the housekeeping to buy the food.» What does housekeeping mean here? | *Money set aside for running a home | The work of cooking a meal | The cleaning department of a hotel | Small tidy-up jobs at work
exercise: «Before we start, here are a few housekeeping notes.» In this meeting, what does housekeeping mean? | The money for the meeting snacks | Cleaning the room where we meet | The work of cooking dinner at home | *Small tidy-up jobs, such as updating files or checking dates
exercise: Rat is a good housekeeper. What does housekeeper suggest? | Someone who keeps animals | *Someone who looks after a home well | Someone who counts money at a bank | A cleaner's bucket
test: «The hotel housekeeping team cleaned every room by noon.» Which meaning of housekeeping is used here? | *The department that cleans the rooms | Small tidy-up jobs at a meeting | The work of reading books | The money for running a home
test: Mole takes pride in his housekeeping. What does he take pride in? | Racing his friends across the field | *Looking after his home: cleaning, cooking and shopping | Reading the paper all day | Playing music for the neighbours
exam: In «the cares and worries and fatigues of housekeeping at home», what does housekeeping mean? | *The everyday work of looking after a home | Money for the shops | A hotel's cleaning team | A tidy-up at a meeting
